+# The Daily Grind
+
+The static page installs cross-window message validation from `page-security.js`.
+Set `ORDERING_ORIGIN` there to the deployment's trusted ordering service origin
+(assumed to be `https://orders.thedailygrind.com`). The check is exact, including
+scheme and non-default port.
+
+Messages use `{ type, url }`:
+
+- The trusted ordering service can send `order:redirect` and `order:open-link`.
+- The designated `#ordering-widget` sandboxed iframe first sends `widget:init`.
+  Its window identity is pinned; only that sender can subsequently send
+  `widget:redirect` and `widget:open-link` with opaque origin `"null"`.
+
+Redirects resolve relative to the page URL and must remain on its exact origin.
+External links must resolve to HTTPS URLs on another origin. Both paths reject
+credentials and malformed URLs. External windows use `noopener,noreferrer`.
+The included hidden widget only initializes the message channel; replace its
+`srcdoc` with widget content while preserving the sandbox and initialization
+protocol. The initialization message contains no sensitive data.
+
+Run `npm test` for the URL and sender-validation regression checks. No server
+or browser is needed.
